  "findings": [
    "REJECTED. The 38 fresh inputs contain 34 independently classified valid Java diagrams. Actual source-only CLI whole-SVG parity improves from 8/34 to 22/34; 12 valid failures remain. The unchanged standing-algorithm diagnostic passes 22/38, retaining four nonpositive outputs as failures. This is bounded semantic support, not acceptance or a scope waiver.",
    "Chronology verified: exact base 0f00130a26b2f300996d0bd427f9e70b4ef10e30 -> account b160f41e2076b98805d4e3c9262a46030394e67c -> implementation 78f06098b74a81d24efcc922b3116d03ad496132 -> evidence candidate 246ff6396b538843143ee9d2cc9a569b67f614dd. Implementation commit cites the earlier account. Production diff is confined to creole.rs; text_render.rs adds only a test. Public Segment/Style/TextBase and TIM are unchanged. No fixture labels, golden reads, tuned coordinates or unexplained layout constants were added.",
    "Bounded model support: pinned CommandCreoleSprite.matchingSize uses Splitter.spritePattern and SpriteUtils.SPRITE_NAME. StripeSimple.modifyStripe flushes pending text before executing a recognized command; addSprite adds an atom only after successful lookup; getAtoms creates one space after restored recursive styles if no atoms exist. Rust private empty segments separate runs even when the following run fills the barrier, and final projection removes remaining empty barriers. Fresh position/repetition/whitespace/closed and EOL style/ASCII and Unicode name/color/delimiter cases support this model; malformed names and tilde/entity escapes remain literal controls.",
    "F1: nested_angle is valid and fails before/after. Java scans unrecognized characters one at a time in StripeSimple.modifyStripe, allowing a recognized <$south> within <bad<$south>>. Rust walk_segments consumes through the first > before handle_tag, then emits the entire unknown tag literally. Java renders A\u00ab$north\u00bbB<bad and >C as two runs, width187; Rust renders a single run containing <$south>, width256. The double-angle portion becomes guillemets in both; the inner command in the unknown-angle portion is the causal divergence. Fix recognition at the scanner boundary, not coordinates.",
    "F2: empty_lines is valid and fails before/after. The new sprite-only stripes correctly become base-font spaces, including the size29 wrapper. The intervening genuinely empty stripe remains an empty text atom of textLength0 instead of Java NBSP width4.1133. creole.rs::parse_segments_inner supplies fallback only when had_barriers; text_render.rs::emit_segments retains the established empty-segment emission path. Dimension and line-position agreement does not make the whole SVG pass.",
    "F3: style_nested consumes both absent commands and matches text, styles, textLength and x coordinates, but all class label baselines are wrong. Java Fir y31.4238 versus Rust28.4795; Elm/Yew Java30.3691 versus Rust27.4258. Exact-candidate class.rs:8456-8524 uses the base name font for line step/ascent before shared emission. This caller obligation remains distinct from shared command recognition. The maker missing_size control also still fails.",
    "F4: wbs and the initially uncertain nested-start legacy_wbs are both valid Java WBS diagrams and fail before/after. WBS::measure at wbs.rs:86-88 measures the raw node label using plantuml_metrics::text_width, while emit_box at156-157 emits through the shared segmenter. After consumption the text atoms match but box/tree widths do not: Java78px versus Rust137px. Port consistent measurement and emission data flow. The fresh title control passes; do not claim all legacy consumers fail. A separate diagnostic using that exact title label proves to_svg_tspans still emits the literal token while parse_segments emits A and B; it is not a product parity metric.",
    "F5: URL labels remain separate unaccepted paths. AtomTextUtils.createAtomTextForUrl scans sprite commands and omits unresolved atoms; Rust creole.rs link arm calls push_literal on the whole label. url_label retains Fir<$north>Elm and expands width191 versus Java128; empty_link retains <$north> and height123 versus Java107. url_after has the pre-existing scheme/italic interaction: Rust protects https:// whereas Java style parsing consumes the // delimiters. Deleting the sprite makes the overall width agree there but text styles/runs still fail.",
    "F6: existing family resolution is real, not universally absent. note_defined and deploy_defined pass before/after, as do all49 valid existing sprite-family controls. Defined class and sequence inline sprites still have no shared registry/resolver: class_defined and seq_defined lose the defined image as well as consuming absent commands and remain whole-output failures. note_defined_scale fails because parse_sprite_segments treats the whole color/scale suffix as part of the lookup key; image missing. note_undefined fails unchanged because a sprite-only note line yields zero-height/no atom in the family-specific resolver, rather than StripeSimple empty fallback. Keep these bounded caller obligations separate and do not overwrite their registry ownership.",
    "F7: regex recognition is not the complete command contract. scale_dot and scale_doubledot match Splitter grammar but Parser.getScale invokes Double.parseDouble before sprite lookup and throws NumberFormatException. Java returns captured crash/error SVGs despite process exit0; Rust silently consumes the command and emits an ordinary diagram. These are runtime-negative references, not positive passes and not malformed literal-tag controls. The explicit negative and empty source controls return welcome/error SVGs with exit200. No returned output was empty; every empty stderr and every nonpositive stdout is retained. Numeric-overflow and zero-scale absent commands are valid and pass after; negative scale is unrecognized/literal and passes both.",
    "Frozen cohorts independently reproduced: retained1730 entries,1651 distinct source/reference pairs,79 duplicate memberships,1609 valid,709 passes both; no lost passes, no model changes,32 panic entries unchanged. Only the two original markup controls change SVG bytes and both still fail. Maker18 has17 valid,3->13 passes; four valid failures retained. Existing sprite50 has49 valid,49 passes both. Fresh38 has no lost pass or model change. These counts do not prove global regression absence beyond measured cohorts.",
    "Original markup_literal and markup_scan still fail whole SVG despite exact projected-source agreement. Java NameAndCodeParser.DISPLAY_WITH_GENERIC and CommandCreateClass extract trailing generic from quoted display. This exact base only splits the id. Separate class candidate68ab512be964e243ae1943f7a9fefd3537091401 already contains split_generic(&mut id).or_else(|| split_generic(&mut label)) at parse/class.rs:993. Read-only confirmation only; no duplicate repair, no combined run, no combined acceptance.",
    "All9731 historical docs/parity-reviews and test-diagrams/perturbations files were independently enumerated from the base and hash-compared to candidate and worktree. Every byte matches. No comparator, baseline, skip, allow-list, target, old evidence or shipping change. Frozen golden gitlink9efdc12fb057bbfecb6a8e2d25d31ec1e5ead19a was empty initially and hydrated through a local shared clone before gates;12550 source files verified. No missing-corpus pass was used.",
    "Required gates ran once on stable exact candidate before checker registration. Parser622, layout41, math10, oracle31 and CLI pipe15 pass. Renderer776 pass and2 failures remain: plain_theme_uses_legacy_class_icon_and_font_defaults; parser_source_identity_matches_java_shadow_id_after_initial_blanks. Exact test-input CLI SVG and YAML are byte-identical before/after; that is attribution evidence, not waiver of failed tests. Main library product diagnostic11179/11251, assisted10497/11251 eligible with1299 skipped of12550, both exit101. Neither library suite is relabeled as an actual CLI count. Guards4/6 exit101 (decimal ratchet, review completeness); clippy exit101 on unchanged component.rs:72 dead code; workspace fmt exit1, touched-file fmt and diff check exit0.",
    "Standing exact-candidate gate635/1666 and matching-environment CLI mapping665/1666 are fully enumerated. Maker gate622/1648 and CLI652/1648 predate registration of the maker18 cases; adding13 passing pairs out of18 accounts for the difference without another repair. The30 include/environment discrepancies remain. Registering this checker adds38 retained pairs; fresh diagnostic22/38 is reported separately, not as a rerun or a new green full gate.",
    "Execution provenance: independent Codex/T3 gpt-6-astra/high checker, same model family as maker but a separate nonimplementing task; no child agents. Private cache and private before/after targets, jobs4; exact CLI builds recorded with revisions and binary hashes. A diagnostic rustc attempt initially failed E0460 due to stale copied oracle dependency metadata while candidate compilation was in progress; preserved, retried successfully after completed gates, with unchanged diagnostic source/comparator. No local JVM/javac, SSH or new remote runner. Only parent-relayed established Monkey Man runner made38 fresh raw -pipe -tsvg calls, zero timeouts. All resource/stream hashes, wrapper/cwd/timezone/env/pinned JAR were independently validated. Java argv is derived from pinned wrapper construction, not process-traced. Historical binary/font/Graphviz and universal Unicode-property/JVM-version equivalence remain unproven."
  ],
